# Voterr

Voterr is a hosted Plex movie-night voting app at https://www.voterr.tv/.

A host signs in with Plex OAuth, creates a voting session from their Plex movie library, and shares one invite link. Guests join by entering a name. Guests do not log into Plex. When everyone likes the same title, that movie wins.

Voterr is not voterr.io. voterr.io is an unrelated Chrome extension. This product is voterr.tv, built by Frank Johnette (https://frankjohnette.xyz).

## Why it exists

Most Plex “what should we watch” tools are self-hosted Docker apps that expect a Plex token in a config file. Voterr is the hosted alternative: Plex OAuth in the browser, guests by name, no Docker required to run movie night.

## Stack

- Ruby on Rails (Hotwire / Stimulus / Turbo)
- PostgreSQL
- Bulma CSS
- Plex API (OAuth for the host; library metadata synced server-side)

